1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,300
Antarctica. Every morning, Mom tucks a pebble into Mochi's backpack. It means "home."

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:06,500
The problem: Mochi has no sense of direction.

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:11,100
That day, the whale ferry came in. Yes. A whale.

4
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:15,500
The smell of fish. Mochi's nose moved before its feet.

5
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:19,100
A whole crate of it.

6
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:21,700
Self-control was never part of the plan.

7
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:24,500
Dinner's over. Food coma begins.

8
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:26,500
Unfortunately, it was departure time.

9
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:31,100
Pelicans are thorough workers. Stamp: to the city.

10
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:33,500
Nobody asked why the crate was snoring.

11
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:36,100
One, two, three, four… five?

12
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:38,700
All that was left was a map.

13
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:42,900
Mochi crossed the ocean. Asleep.

14
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:47,500
And then, lights Mochi had never seen.

15
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:51,500
Thud. Mochi woke up, and the light looked… wrong.

16
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:58,100
Outside the box, there was no snow.

17
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:00,100
None under its feet, either.

18
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:04,100
The only ride home just left. Can Mochi find the way back? (To be continued)

